    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 4 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win the pot by having the highest hand (or best qualifying low hand in Hi-Lo deals) at showdown, or by forcing all opponents to fold.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Format Roll**: Dealer rolls die: 1-2 = 4-card, 3-4 = 5-card, 5-6 = 6-card. High/Low is determined by house rule or second roll. 2. **Betting**: Standard Pot Limit structure. 3. **Hand Construction**: You MUST use exactly two cards from your hand and exactly three cards from the community board to form a five-card hand.',
      'Scoring example: Standard poker pot mechanics. In High deals, best hand wins entire pot. In Hi-Lo deals, pot is split between best high hand and best qualifying low hand. Highest chip total at the end of the session or tournament..',
